            <title>[LU-21282] sanity-sec test_31: lod_sub_prep_llog() ASSERTION( !ctxt-&gt;loc_handle ) failed in lod_sub_recovery_thread after MDT remount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21282</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d43d566e-f4e8-4edc-aea7-848d1642bcf0" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d43d566e-f4e8-4edc-aea7-848d1642bcf0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_31 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;onyx-156vm264 crashed during sanity-sec test_31
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62.1&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137262" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137262&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.62.1&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137262" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137262&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_31 crashed the MDS (onyx-156vm264, el10.2 ZFS, review-dne-zfs-part-4, kernel 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2_lustre) right after remounting lustre-MDT0001 and lustre-MDT0003:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LustreError: (lod_sub_object.c:982:lod_sub_prep_llog()) ASSERTION( !ctxt-&amp;gt;loc_handle ) failed:&lt;br/&gt;
LustreError: (lod_sub_object.c:982:lod_sub_prep_llog()) LBUG&lt;br/&gt;
Comm: lod0001_rec0003&lt;br/&gt;
  lod_sub_prep_llog+0xacb/0xae0 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;lod&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
  lod_sub_recovery_thread+0xba/0xc50 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;lod&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
  kthread&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the double initialization of a sub llog that &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18460" title="ASSERTION( !ctxt-&amp;gt;loc_handle ) in lod_sub_prep_llog" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18460"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18460&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (Resolved Fixed, 2025-05-27, commit 0c364cf6f7 "lod: avoid double llog initialization") fixed. That fix is in the tested code, so this is a recurrence on the recovery thread path. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18460" title="ASSERTION( !ctxt-&amp;gt;loc_handle ) in lod_sub_prep_llog" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18460"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18460&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was resolved more than 180 days ago, hence a new ticket.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not the patch's: the tested change (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19054" title="allow limiting the number of clients connected to the filesystem" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19054"&gt;LU-19054&lt;/a&gt; client_limit, review 61943 patchset 41) touches no lod, osp or llog code, exempts server connections from the limit, and leaves client_limit at -1 in this test. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21139" title="conf-sanity test_153c: class_decref_free() ASSERTION OBDF_ATTACHED at MDT umount, obd_zombid" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21139"&gt;LU-21139&lt;/a&gt; (class_decref_free at umount) is a different assertion, and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19686" title="Crash on lod_sub_recovery_thread due to NULL pointer dereference" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19686"&gt;LU-19686&lt;/a&gt; (NULL dereference in lod_sub_recovery_thread) a different failure. Rare: 1 branch failure with this signature in 30 days, 0 of 237 review runs of this test group failed in the previous 30 days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d43d566e-f4e8-4edc-aea7-848d1642bcf0" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/d43d566e-f4e8-4edc-aea7-848d1642bcf0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subtest: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/1575ef1d-3223-4705-8abb-4fa7dfd5e3c6" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/1575ef1d-3223-4705-8abb-4fa7dfd5e3c6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-61943-ps41-b01ead671abc on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/61943" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/61943&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
